A simple consultation cost €75, with no emergency, no injections or products administered, plus €28 for a blood test.

At that price, I expected a practitioner fully focused on the animal and a clear, scientific explanation. What I found:

a blood-soaked compress left on the floor, clearly from the previous appointment. My puppy went and licked it without the practitioner seeming to mind;
a veterinarian who couldn't remember if she had examined my dog's heart, a Doberman, a breed known for its heart problems;
when I asked about the cause of a bump, the first response was, "It comes and goes, it's common in this breed," then, when I pressed her, "we don't really know";

products being pushed for sale during the consultation.

While out walking, many dog ​​owners in the neighborhood had strongly advised me against this clinic. I now understand why.
